britain has authorized another vaccine  for emergency use  one of the scientists who helped develop  the oxford astrazeneca vaccine calls it  a vaccine for the world it is likely to  be approved in the u.s sometime  next year charlie dagetta is in london  this morning  how is the news being received there  charlie david it has been hailed as a  vaccine  that will transform the fight against  covid a global game changer  and not a minute too soon in a country  and a world  under siege cheap easy to store in  transport and will vastly accelerate the  vaccination program  crucially regulators decided the first  dose provides  good immunity good enough to prevent  hospitalization  and serious disease a second dose  follows up to 12 weeks later  unlike other vaccines that need a 28-day  booster  that extended timeline allows for the  production of more vaccine  effectively doubling the number of  people who can get vaccinated in the  short term  the number that will be ready for next  week is in the  hundreds of thousands and then the  numbers  increase significantly after that the  urgency could not be greater  lines of ambulances with covid patients  inside have been  stacked up outside hospitals as britain  recorded its highest one-day  case total since the pandemic began  unlike the pfizer biontech vaccine  currently administered here  the oxford astrazeneca vaccine never  needs to be kept at deep freeze  temperatures  making it easier to administer in mass  vaccination centers  not just in the uk but eventually around  the globe  now the united states has put 1.2  billion dollars behind this vaccine in  exchange for at least 300 million doses  the question now is whether the fda  speeds up their own approval process  after the decisions made here adriana  charlie dagetta in london thank you
 

